File: ax-plots.info,  Node: Function animate object [param lo hi] / animate object [param lo hi n],  Next: Reactive plots,  Up: Animation and Interaction

 -- Function: animate (OBJECT, [PARAM, LO, HI]) / ANIMATE (OBJECT,
          [PARAM, LO, HI, N])
     Animates a draw object over a parameter.  Use it inside ‘ax_draw2d’
     or ‘ax_draw3d’ in place of the object: ‘object’ is drawn at ‘n’
     values of ‘param’, evenly spaced from ‘lo’ to ‘hi’ inclusive (60 by
     default), and the plot gets a play button and a slider to scrub
     through them.

     ‘param’ must be a symbol that ‘object’ depends on, such as ‘k’ in
     ‘explicit(sin(k*x), x, -%pi, %pi)’.  Every ‘animate’ in one plot
     must use the same ‘[param, lo, hi, n]’; objects outside ‘animate’
     stay fixed.

* Menu:

     * Examples::
     * What can be animated::
     * Playback options::

1.4.1 Examples
--------------

/* A wave changing frequency */
ax_draw2d(animate(explicit(sin(k*x), x, -%pi, %pi), [k, 0.5, 3, 40]))$

/* Several animated objects share one parameter; the circle stays fixed */
ax_draw2d(
  parametric(cos(s), sin(s), s, 0, 2*%pi, color="gray"),
  animate(vector([0, 0], [cos(t), sin(t)], color="red"), [t, 0, 2*%pi, 48]),
  animate(label([t, 1.25*cos(t), 1.25*sin(t)]), [t, 0, 2*%pi, 48]),
  aspect_ratio=true, xrange=[-1.6, 1.6], yrange=[-1.6, 1.6], slider_label="t"
)$

/* A surface in 3D */
ax_draw3d(animate(
  explicit(sin(k*x)*cos(y), x, -%pi, %pi, y, -%pi, %pi), [k, 0.5, 2.0]),
  colorscale="Viridis")$

* Menu:

* What can be animated::
