File: ax-plots.info,  Node: What can be animated,  Next: Playback options,  Up: 

1.4.1.1 What can be animated
............................

   • Curves, points, surfaces and the other trace objects, in 2D and 3D.
     The object must produce the same number of traces at every frame.
   • In 2D, also ‘label’, ‘vector’ and shapes (‘rectangle’, ‘ellipse’,
     ‘hline’, ‘vline’).  They are rebuilt for each frame and jump
     between frames rather than tweening.  A label whose text is a
     float, such as ‘label([t, x, y])’, shows it to 3 significant
     figures.
   • ‘animate’ and ‘reactive’ signals can't be combined in one plot.

With the ‘numerics’ package loaded, an animated 2D ‘explicit’ is sampled
for all frames at once by ‘numerics’' ‘compile_grid’, which is several
times faster for long animations.  This needs a ‘numerics’ with
‘compile_grid’ (published to the mxpm index on 2026-10-19).


File: ax-plots.info,  Node: Playback options,  Prev: What can be animated,  Up: 

1.4.1.2 Playback options
........................

These are plot options, given alongside ‘title’ or ‘xrange’:

Option              Default                Description
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
‘fps’               12                     Frames per second when
                                           playing
‘transition_duration’1000 / ‘fps’ ms       Tween between frames; ‘0’
                                           steps without tweening
‘slider_label’      the parameter's name   Text before the value on the
                                           slider

An animation plays once per press of the play button.  ‘loop’ is not
implemented, and giving it is an error.

Playing an animation needs a host that registers Plotly frames.  Aximar
does from its June 2026 ‘master’ onwards; release v0.14.0 shows the
controls but they do nothing.

See also: ‘ax_draw2d’, ‘ax_draw3d’


