  ax_heatmap(sin(x)*cos(y), x, -%pi, %pi, y, -%pi, %pi),
  colorscale="Hot"
)$

1.5.1.7 Relevant Options
........................

Option              Default                Description
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
‘colorscale’        auto                   Color scale: ‘"Viridis"’,
                                           ‘"Hot"’, ‘"Blues"’, etc.
‘showscale’         auto                   Show/hide the color bar
‘nticks’            50                     Grid resolution (expression
                                           form only)
‘name’              auto                   Legend entry
‘opacity’           1.0                    Trace opacity

See also: ‘ax_draw2d’, ‘ax_contour’


File: ax-plots.info,  Node: Function ax_box data / ax_box data category,  Next: Function ax_violin data / ax_violin data category,  Prev: Function ax_heatmap z_matrix,  Up: Statistical Charts

 -- Function: ax_box (DATA) / AX_BOX (DATA, CATEGORY)
     Box plot of a list of numbers (or an ndarray).  Use inside
     ‘ax_draw2d’.  With a ‘category’ string, the box is placed at that
     position on the x-axis, so several ‘ax_box’ objects with different
     categories sit side by side.

* Menu:

     * Examples::
     * Relevant Options::

1.5.1.8 Examples
................

ax_draw2d(ax_box([2.1, 2.5, 2.8, 3.0, 3.2, 3.9, 5.6]))$

/* Two groups, with every point shown and the mean marked */
ax_draw2d(
  ax_box([5, 7, 8, 9, 12, 15], "control"),
  ax_box([8, 10, 11, 13, 14, 21], "treated"),
  boxpoints=all, boxmean=true, showlegend=false
)$

1.5.1.9 Relevant Options
........................

Option              Default                Description
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
‘color’             auto                   Box colour
‘boxpoints’         outliers               Points drawn beside the box:
                                           ‘all’, ‘outliers’ (or a
                                           Plotly value as a string)
‘boxmean’           false                  ‘true’ marks the mean; ‘sd’
                                           also shows the standard
                                           deviation
‘name’              ‘"box"’                Legend entry

See also: ‘ax_violin’, ‘ax_histogram’, ‘ax_draw2d’


